    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "We call such a connected sum of quiver settings thin if d i = 1. In the following, the symbol ↔ denotes an arrow of either orientation."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 44,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 126.0, 169.0, 487.333, 219.0 ],
    "font" : "CMTI10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Theorem 4.2. For a connected quiver setting ( Q, d ) , the representation space R d ( Q ) is a spherical variety under the action of B d ⊂ G d if and only if ( Q, d ) is a thin connect sum of quiver settings with Q of the form 1 ↔ 2 ↔ 3 , and d = ( m,n, 1) or d = ( m, 2 ,n ) ."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
