    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "(1) If Q contains a cycle, then R d ( Q ) even admits inﬁnitely many G d -orbits, since there are already inﬁnitely many isomorphism classes of representations of dimension vector (1 ,..., 1) for any cycle quiver. Thus we can assume Q to be a tree."
  } ]
